{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_RtPHdWwugcw5iWsswLDDyUPg","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# session-protocol Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→Define the session lifecycle protocol for SE 3.0 agents. This spec governs progressive startup (se3 status → progress.md → scope determination), execution boundaries, shutdown procedures, and tool-enforced progress tracking across sessions.\n     5→## Requirements\n     6→### Requirement: Session Startup Protocol\n     7→The system SHALL define a progressive session startup protocol. The agent MUST locate current state with minimal context, then load more on demand.\n     8→\n     9→Startup steps:\n    10→1. Verify `openspec` CLI is available; if not, ask the human to install it. If available but `openspec/` directory does not exist, run `openspec init`.\n    11→2. Run `se3 status` for computed project state (git, collab, human-calls)\n    12→3. Read `head -50 progress.md` + `git log --oneline -5`\n    13→4. Scan `human-calls/` for responded but unprocessed requests\n    14→5. Check `openspec/changes/` for active changes and `openspec/specs/` for current capabilities\n    15→6. Determine session scope based on progress \"next steps\" + active changes\n    16→7. Load additional files only when the task requires them\n    17→\n    18→If step 3 finds no progress.md and no git history → **first-time bootstrap**:\n    19→- Ask the human (sync human call): \"What should this project do?\"\n    20→- Create an openspec change from the response (proposal captures the intent)\n    21→- Create `progress.md`\n    22→\n    23→#### Scenario: OpenSpec not installed\n    24→- **WHEN** agent starts a session and `openspec` command is not found\n    25→- **THEN** agent asks the human to install it via sync human call and does not proceed with spec-related work until resolved\n    26→\n    27→#### Scenario: OpenSpec not initialized\n    28→- **WHEN** agent starts a session and `openspec` is available but `openspec/` directory does not exist\n    29→- **THEN** agent runs `openspec init` before proceeding\n    30→\n    31→#### Scenario: Mature project startup\n    32→- **WHEN** agent starts a session with existing progress.md and git history\n    33→- **THEN** agent runs `se3 status`, reads progress.md and git log, then determines scope without reading all spec files upfront\n    34→\n    35→#### Scenario: First-time bootstrap\n    36→- **WHEN** agent starts a session with no progress.md and no git history\n    37→- **THEN** agent asks the human what to build via human call, creates an openspec change from the response\n    38→\n    39→#### Scenario: On-demand deep loading\n    40→- **WHEN** agent needs details about a specific capability during execution\n    41→- **THEN** agent reads the relevant spec file at that point, not during startup\n    42→\n    43→### Requirement: Session Execution Boundary\n    44→Each session MUST focus on a limited scope of work and MUST NOT attempt to complete too many tasks in a single session.\n    45→\n    46→#### Scenario: Session scope limitation\n    47→- **WHEN** the agent has determined the work scope through the startup protocol\n    48→- **THEN** the agent only executes tasks within that scope and does not actively expand the scope\n    49→\n    50→### Requirement: Session Shutdown Protocol\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdb5c0cc-8986-4ab3-a245-a310803fdfe0","uuid":"e8b5c2ba-da59-43ff-97a3-a3254cb5e318","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/openspec-cli-commands/openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md","content":"# session-protocol Specification\n\n## Purpose\nDefine the session lifecycle protocol for SE 3.0 agents. This spec governs progressive startup (se3 status → progress.md → scope determination), execution boundaries, shutdown procedures, and tool-enforced progress tracking across sessions.\n## Requirements\n### Requirement: Session Startup Protocol\nThe system SHALL define a progressive session startup protocol. The agent MUST locate current state with minimal context, then load more on demand.\n\nStartup steps:\n1. Verify `openspec` CLI is available; if not, ask the human to install it. If available but `openspec/` directory does not exist, run `openspec init`.\n2. Run `se3 status` for computed project state (git, collab, human-calls)\n3. Read `head -50 progress.md` + `git log --oneline -5`\n4. Scan `human-calls/` for responded but unprocessed requests\n5. Check `openspec/changes/` for active changes and `openspec/specs/` for current capabilities\n6. Determine session scope based on progress \"next steps\" + active changes\n7. Load additional files only when the task requires them\n\nIf step 3 finds no progress.md and no git history → **first-time bootstrap**:\n- Ask the human (sync human call): \"What should this project do?\"\n- Create an openspec change from the response (proposal captures the intent)\n- Create `progress.md`\n\n#### Scenario: OpenSpec not installed\n- **WHEN** agent starts a session and `openspec` command is not found\n- **THEN** agent asks the human to install it via sync human call and does not proceed with spec-related work until resolved\n\n#### Scenario: OpenSpec not initialized\n- **WHEN** agent starts a session and `openspec` is available but `openspec/` directory does not exist\n- **THEN** agent runs `openspec init` before proceeding\n\n#### Scenario: Mature project startup\n- **WHEN** agent starts a session with existing progress.md and git history\n- **THEN** agent runs `se3 status`, reads progress.md and git log, then determines scope without reading all spec files upfront\n\n#### Scenario: First-time bootstrap\n- **WHEN** agent starts a session with no progress.md and no git history\n- **THEN** agent asks the human what to build via human call, creates an openspec change from the response\n\n#### Scenario: On-demand deep loading\n- **WHEN** agent needs details about a specific capability during execution\n- **THEN** agent reads the relevant spec file at that point, not during startup\n\n### Requirement: Session Execution Boundary\nEach session MUST focus on a limited scope of work and MUST NOT attempt to complete too many tasks in a single session.\n\n#### Scenario: Session scope limitation\n- **WHEN** the agent has determined the work scope through the startup protocol\n- **THEN** the agent only executes tasks within that scope and does not actively expand the scope\n\n### Requirement: Session Shutdown Protocol","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":116}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_tttyabtVNfC6e1tzJLX6lEaQ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"SE 3.0 init command - Initialize a new SE 3.0 project.\"\"\"\n     2→\n     3→import os\n     4→import hashlib\n     5→from datetime import datetime\n     6→from pathlib import Path\n     7→import shutil\n     8→import typer\n     9→\n    10→from ..utils import copy_file\n    11→from .. import SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION\n    12→\n    13→app = typer.Typer()\n    14→\n    15→\n    16→def compute_checksum(content: str) -> str:\n    17→    \"\"\"Compute SHA-256 checksum of content.\"\"\"\n    18→    return hashlib.sha256(content.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n    19→\n    20→\n    21→def get_project_name() -> str:\n    22→    \"\"\"Get project name from current directory.\"\"\"\n    23→    return Path.cwd().name\n    24→\n    25→\n    26→def get_current_date() -> str:\n    27→    \"\"\"Get current date in YYYY-MM-DD format.\"\"\"\n    28→    return datetime.now().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n    29→\n    30→\n    31→def initialize_project(\n    32→    force: bool = False,\n    33→    offline: bool = False,\n    34→    with_config: bool = False,\n    35→    se3_version: str = SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION,\n    36→) -> None:\n    37→    \"\"\"\n    38→    Initialize an SE 3.0 project.\n    39→\n    40→    Args:\n    41→        force: Reinitialize even if already initialized\n    42→        offline: Use local templates without network\n    43→        with_config: Create se3.config.yaml\n    44→        se3_version: SE 3.0 version to use\n    45→    \"\"\"\n    46→    # Check if already initialized\n    47→    claude_dir = Path(\".claude\")\n    48→    if claude_dir.exists():\n    49→        if not force:\n    50→            typer.echo(\n    51→                typer.style(\n    52→                    \"Error: Project already initialized. Use --force to reinitialize.\",\n    53→                    fg=typer.colors.RED,\n    54→                )\n    55→            )\n    56→            raise typer.Exit(1)\n    57→        # Force mode: only overwrite SE3.md and CLAUDE.md, preserve everything else\n    58→        typer.echo(\"Force mode: overwriting SE3.md and CLAUDE.md in .claude/\")\n    59→\n    60→    # Create .claude directory (no-op if it already exists)\n    61→    claude_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    62→\n    63→    # 1. Create SE3.md (from template with version and metadata)\n    64→    # Locate template directory relative to package location\n    65→    project_root = Path(__file__).parent.parent.parent.parent\n    66→    templates_dir = project_root / \"output\"\n    67→\n    68→    se3_template_path = templates_dir / \"SE3.md.template\"\n    69→    se3_content = se3_template_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    70→\n    71→    # Add metadata\n    72→    metadata = (\n    73→        f\"<!-- Generated on {get_current_date()} -->\\n\"\n    74→        f\"<!-- SE3 Version: {se3_version} -->\\n\"\n    75→        f\"<!-- Checksum: {compute_checksum(se3_content)} -->\\n\\n\"\n    76→    )\n    77→\n    78→    se3_content = metadata + se3_content\n    79→\n    80→    se3_path = claude_dir / \"SE3.md\"\n    81→    se3_path.write_text(se3_content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    82→    typer.echo(f\"Created {se3_path}\")\n    83→\n    84→    # 2. Create CLAUDE.md from minimal template\n    85→    minimal_template_path = templates_dir / \"CLAUDE.minimal.md.template\"\n    86→    claude_content = minimal_template_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    87→\n    88→    # Replace placeholders\n    89→    claude_content = claude_content.replace(\"{{PROJECT_NAME}}\", get_project_name())\n    90→\n    91→    claude_path = claude_dir / \"CLAUDE.md\"\n    92→    claude_path.write_text(claude_content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    93→    typer.echo(f\"Created {claude_path}\")\n    94→\n    95→    # 3. Create se3.config.yaml if --with-config flag\n    96→    if with_config:\n    97→        config_template_path = Path(\"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/output/se3.config.yaml\")\n    98→        config_path = Path(\"se3.config.yaml\")\n    99→        copy_file(config_template_path, config_path)\n   100→        typer.echo(f\"Created {config_path}\")\n   101→\n   102→    # 4. Create other required directories\n   103→    for dir_name in [\"human-calls\", \"openspec/specs\", \"openspec/changes\", \"output\"]:\n   104→        dir_path = Path(dir_name)\n   105→        dir_path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   106→\n   107→    # 5. Install SE3 workflow skills to .claude/commands/se3/\n   108→    skills_source = templates_dir / \"commands\" / \"se3\"\n   109→    skills_dest = claude_dir / \"commands\" / \"se3\"\n   110→    if skills_source.exists():\n   111→        skills_dest.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   112→        for skill_file in skills_source.glob(\"*.md\"):\n   113→            dest_file = skills_dest / skill_file.name\n   114→            shutil.copy2(skill_file, dest_file)\n   115→            typer.echo(f\"Installed skill: {dest_file}\")\n   116→\n   117→    typer.echo(\n   118→        typer.style(\n   119→            \"SE 3.0 project initialized successfully!\",\n   120→            fg=typer.colors.GREEN,\n   121→        )\n   122→    )\n   123→    typer.echo(\"\\nStart working with: /se3:start\")\n   124→\n   125→\n   126→@app.command()\n   127→def init(\n   128→    force: bool = typer.Option(\n   129→        False,\n   130→        \"--force\",\n   131→        \"-f\",\n   132→        help=\"Reinitialize even if already initialized\",\n   133→    ),\n   134→    offline: bool = typer.Option(\n   135→        False,\n   136→        \"--offline\",\n   137→        \"-o\",\n   138→        help=\"Use local templates without network\",\n   139→    ),\n   140→    with_config: bool = typer.Option(\n   141→        False,\n   142→        \"--with-config\",\n   143→        \"-c\",\n   144→        help=\"Create se3.config.yaml\",\n   145→    ),\n   146→    se3_version: str = typer.Option(\n   147→        SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION,\n   148→        \"--se3-version\",\n   149→        \"-v\",\n   150→        help=\"Specify SE3 version to use\",\n   151→    ),\n   152→) -> None:\n   153→    \"\"\"Initialize a new SE 3.0 project.\"\"\"\n   154→    try:\n   155→        initialize_project(force, offline, with_config, se3_version)\n   156→    except Exception as e:\n   157→        typer.echo(\n   158→            typer.style(\n   159→                f\"Error during initialization: {str(e)}\",\n   160→                fg=typer.colors.RED,\n   161→            )\n   162→        )\n   163→        raise typer.Exit(1)\n   164→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdb5c0cc-8986-4ab3-a245-a310803fdfe0","uuid":"5dcb0d42-f74b-43c3-8aa9-ab2e8f49220d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/openspec-cli-commands/tools/se3_tools/commands/init.py","content":"\"\"\"SE 3.0 init command - Initialize a new SE 3.0 project.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nimport hashlib\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nimport typer\n\nfrom ..utils import copy_file\nfrom .. import SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION\n\napp = typer.Typer()\n\n\ndef compute_checksum(content: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Compute SHA-256 checksum of content.\"\"\"\n    return hashlib.sha256(content.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef get_project_name() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Get project name from current directory.\"\"\"\n    return Path.cwd().name\n\n\ndef get_current_date() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Get current date in YYYY-MM-DD format.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n\n\ndef initialize_project(\n    force: bool = False,\n    offline: bool = False,\n    with_config: bool = False,\n    se3_version: str = SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Initialize an SE 3.0 project.\n\n    Args:\n        force: Reinitialize even if already initialized\n        offline: Use local templates without network\n        with_config: Create se3.config.yaml\n        se3_version: SE 3.0 version to use\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check if already initialized\n    claude_dir = Path(\".claude\")\n    if claude_dir.exists():\n        if not force:\n            typer.echo(\n                typer.style(\n                    \"Error: Project already initialized. Use --force to reinitialize.\",\n                    fg=typer.colors.RED,\n                )\n            )\n            raise typer.Exit(1)\n        # Force mode: only overwrite SE3.md and CLAUDE.md, preserve everything else\n        typer.echo(\"Force mode: overwriting SE3.md and CLAUDE.md in .claude/\")\n\n    # Create .claude directory (no-op if it already exists)\n    claude_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # 1. Create SE3.md (from template with version and metadata)\n    # Locate template directory relative to package location\n    project_root = Path(__file__).parent.parent.parent.parent\n    templates_dir = project_root / \"output\"\n\n    se3_template_path = templates_dir / \"SE3.md.template\"\n    se3_content = se3_template_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    # Add metadata\n    metadata = (\n        f\"<!-- Generated on {get_current_date()} -->\\n\"\n        f\"<!-- SE3 Version: {se3_version} -->\\n\"\n        f\"<!-- Checksum: {compute_checksum(se3_content)} -->\\n\\n\"\n    )\n\n    se3_content = metadata + se3_content\n\n    se3_path = claude_dir / \"SE3.md\"\n    se3_path.write_text(se3_content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    typer.echo(f\"Created {se3_path}\")\n\n    # 2. Create CLAUDE.md from minimal template\n    minimal_template_path = templates_dir / \"CLAUDE.minimal.md.template\"\n    claude_content = minimal_template_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    # Replace placeholders\n    claude_content = claude_content.replace(\"{{PROJECT_NAME}}\", get_project_name())\n\n    claude_path = claude_dir / \"CLAUDE.md\"\n    claude_path.write_text(claude_content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    typer.echo(f\"Created {claude_path}\")\n\n    # 3. Create se3.config.yaml if --with-config flag\n    if with_config:\n        config_template_path = Path(\"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/output/se3.config.yaml\")\n        config_path = Path(\"se3.config.yaml\")\n        copy_file(config_template_path, config_path)\n        typer.echo(f\"Created {config_path}\")\n\n    # 4. Create other required directories\n    for dir_name in [\"human-calls\", \"openspec/specs\", \"openspec/changes\", \"output\"]:\n        dir_path = Path(dir_name)\n        dir_path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # 5. Install SE3 workflow skills to .claude/commands/se3/\n    skills_source = templates_dir / \"commands\" / \"se3\"\n    skills_dest = claude_dir / \"commands\" / \"se3\"\n    if skills_source.exists():\n        skills_dest.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        for skill_file in skills_source.glob(\"*.md\"):\n            dest_file = skills_dest / skill_file.name\n            shutil.copy2(skill_file, dest_file)\n            typer.echo(f\"Installed skill: {dest_file}\")\n\n    typer.echo(\n        typer.style(\n            \"SE 3.0 project initialized successfully!\",\n            fg=typer.colors.GREEN,\n        )\n    )\n    typer.echo(\"\\nStart working with: /se3:start\")\n\n\n@app.command()\ndef init(\n    force: bool = typer.Option(\n        False,\n        \"--force\",\n        \"-f\",\n        help=\"Reinitialize even if already initialized\",\n    ),\n    offline: bool = typer.Option(\n        False,\n        \"--offline\",\n        \"-o\",\n        help=\"Use local templates without network\",\n    ),\n    with_config: bool = typer.Option(\n        False,\n        \"--with-config\",\n        \"-c\",\n        help=\"Create se3.config.yaml\",\n    ),\n    se3_version: str = typer.Option(\n        SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION,\n        \"--se3-version\",\n        \"-v\",\n        help=\"Specify SE3 version to use\",\n    ),\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Initialize a new SE 3.0 project.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        initialize_project(force, offline, with_config, se3_version)\n    except Exception as e:\n        typer.echo(\n            typer.style(\n                f\"Error during initialization: {str(e)}\",\n                fg=typer.colors.RED,\n            )\n        )\n        raise typer.Exit(1)\n","numLines":164,"startLine":1,"totalLines":164}}}
